			"140": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 3: MERGING TEXTURES\n\nIn this example we have a Rhombus shape that is randomly moved across the screen with X\/Y values coming from the two Perlin Generator nodes.\nWe render the shape to a texture with a semi-transparent color.\nNext we use the Ring Buffer to create a trail effect, this is done by storing 10 textures.\n\nNext we want to apply the Color Offset effect to the entire output.\nFor this reason we first Merge the collection of textures down to a single texture and apply the effect afterwards.\n\nNote that because we are using textures the Merge node allows us to use different stretching options for the textures in the merge."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 779.3759765625,
					"width": 1985.713134765625,
					"x": -285.374755859375,
					"y": 1356.9659423828125
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "fff26eb5",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment"
			},
			"71": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "MERGE\n\nThe Merge node merges the incoming collection to a single channel.\nDepending on the type in the collection (strings, texture, shape etc), the merge node will behave differently.\n\nIn this patch we'll go through all the use cases for the Merge node."
					}
				},
